Enforcement Decree of the Framework Act on Railroad Industry Development

Article 1 (Purpose)
The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters delegated by the Framework Act on Railroad Industry Development and matters necessary for its enforcement.

Article 2 (Railroad Facilities)
"Facilities prescribed by Presidential Decree" in subparagraph 2 (g) of Article 3 of the Framework Act on Railroad Industry Development (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") means the following facilities: <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013>
1. Facilities used during the relevant project period to process, assemble, transport, or store materials necessary for railroad construction, maintenance, and repair;
2. Access roads, parking lots, outdoor storage yards, earth and stone extraction sites, and spoil disposal sites used for railroad construction, maintenance, and repair works, and facilities necessary for their installation or operation;
3. Equipment used during the relevant project period for railroad construction, maintenance, and repair, and facilities for maintaining, inspecting, or repairing that equipment;
4. Other facilities determined by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport as necessary for railroad construction, maintenance, repair, and operation, such as railroad safety facilities and guidance facilities.

Article 3 (Content of the Master Plan for Railroad Industry Development)
"Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 5 (2) 8 of the Act means the following matters: <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013>
1. Targets for the share of transportation carried by railroad;
2. Matters concerning railroad safety and railroad services;
3. Matters concerning transportation links with other modes of transport;
4. Matters concerning international cooperation and entry into overseas markets in the railroad industry;
5. The implementation system for railroad industry policies;
6. Other matters concerning the promotion and development of the railroad industry that the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport deems necessary.

Article 4 (Minor Amendments to the Master Plan for Railroad Industry Development)
"Minor amendments prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the latter part of Article 5 (4) of the Act means the following amendments:
1. An amendment within one percent of the scale of a railroad facilities investment project;
2. An amendment within one percent of the total investment cost of a railroad facilities investment project;
3. An amendment to the period of a railroad facilities investment project within a range of two years.

Article 5 (Procedures for Formulating Implementation Plans for Railroad Industry Development, etc.)
(1) The heads of relevant administrative agencies shall submit the implementation plan for the relevant year under Article 5 (6) of the Act to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport by the end of November of the preceding year. <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013>
(2) The heads of relevant administrative agencies shall submit the implementation performance of the previous year's implementation plan to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport by the end of February each year. <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013>

Article 6 (Composition of the Railroad Industry Committee)
(1) The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall serve as the chairperson of the Railroad Industry Committee under Article 6 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Committee"). <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013>
(2) The following persons shall serve as members of the Committee: <Amended on February 29, 2008; July 12, 2010; March 23, 2013; November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017; September 10, 2020; October 1, 2025; December 30, 2025>
1. The Vice Minister of Finance and Economy, Vice Minister of Science and ICT, Vice Minister of Education, Vice Minister of the Interior and Safety, Vice Minister of Trade and Industry, Vice Minister of Employment and Labor, Vice Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, Vice Minister of Oceans and Fisheries, Vice Minister of Planning and Budget, and Vice Chairperson of the Fair Trade Commission;
2. The Chairperson of Korea National Railway (hereinafter referred to as "Korea National Railway") under Article 20 (3) of the Act;
3. The President of the Korea Railroad Corporation (hereinafter referred to as the "Korea Railroad Corporation") under Article 21 (3) of the Act;
4. Persons commissioned by the chairperson of the Committee from among persons with extensive expertise and experience in the railroad industry.
(3) The term of office of a member under paragraph (2) 4 shall be two years and may be renewed.

Article 6-2 (Dismissal of Members)
The chairperson of the Committee may dismiss a member under Article 6 (2) 4 in any of the following cases:
1. Where the member becomes unable to perform the duties of the office due to a physical or mental disability;
2. Where the member has engaged in misconduct related to the duties of the office;
3. Where the member is deemed unsuitable due to neglect of duties, impairment of dignity, or other grounds;
4. Where the member personally expresses that it is difficult to perform the duties of the office.

Article 7 (Duties of the Chairperson of the Committee)
(1) The chairperson of the Committee shall represent the Committee and oversee its affairs.
(2) Where the chairperson of the Committee is unable to perform the duties of the office due to unavoidable circumstances, a member designated in advance by the chairperson shall act on the chairperson's behalf.

Article 8 (Meetings)
(1) The chairperson of the Committee shall convene meetings of the Committee and preside over them.
(2) Resolutions at meetings of the Committee shall require the attendance of a majority of the incumbent members and the affirmative vote of a majority of the members present.
(3) The Committee shall prepare and keep minutes of its meetings.

Article 9 (Secretary)
The Committee shall have one secretary, who shall be designated by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport from among public officials of that Ministry. <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013>

Article 10 (Composition of the Working Committee, etc.)
(1) A Working Committee shall be established within the Committee to conduct working-level reviews of matters to be deliberated upon or coordinated by the Committee and matters delegated by the Committee.
(2) The Working Committee shall consist of not more than 20 members, including its chairperson.
(3) The chairperson of the Working Committee shall be designated by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport from among Grade 3 public officials or public officials in general service belonging to the Senior Civil Service of that Ministry. <Amended on June 12, 2006; February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013>
(4) The following persons shall serve as members of the Working Committee: <Amended on June 12, 2006; February 29, 2008; July 12, 2010; March 23, 2013; November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017; September 10, 2020; October 1, 2025; December 30, 2025>
1. One person from each of the Ministry of Finance and Economy, Ministry of Science and ICT, Ministry of Education, Ministry of the Interior and Safety, Ministry of Trade and Industry, Ministry of Employment and Labor, Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries, Ministry of Planning and Budget, and Fair Trade Commission, designated by the head of the relevant institution from among its Grade 3 public officials, Grade 4 public officials, or public officials in general service belonging to the Senior Civil Service;
2. One person designated by the Chairperson of Korea National Railway from among its executive officers and employees;
3. One person designated by the President of the Korea Railroad Corporation from among its executive officers and employees;
4. Persons commissioned by the chairperson of the Working Committee from among persons with extensive expertise and experience in the railroad industry.
(5) The term of office of a member under paragraph (4) 4 shall be two years and may be renewed.
(6) The Working Committee shall have one secretary, who shall be designated by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport from among public officials of that Ministry. <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013>
(7) Article 8 shall apply mutatis mutandis to meetings of the Working Committee.

Article 10-2 (Dismissal of Members of the Working Committee, etc.)
(1) A person who has designated a member pursuant to Article 10 (4) 1 through 3 may withdraw that designation where the member falls under any of the following subparagraphs:
1. Where the member becomes unable to perform the duties of the office due to a physical or mental disability;
2. Where the member has engaged in misconduct related to the duties of the office;
3. Where the member is deemed unsuitable due to neglect of duties, impairment of dignity, or other grounds;
4. Where the member personally expresses that it is difficult to perform the duties of the office.
(2) The chairperson of the Working Committee may dismiss a member under Article 10 (4) 4 where the member falls under any subparagraph of paragraph (1).

Article 11 (Composition of the Railroad Industry Structural Reform Planning Group, etc.)
(1) A Railroad Industry Structural Reform Planning Group (hereinafter referred to as the "Planning Group") shall be established under the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport to support the activities of the Committee and to support and perform the following duties related to structural reform of the railroad industry and other railroad policies: <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013>
1. Formulation of the master plan for railroad industry structural reform and detailed implementation plans for each sector;
2. Reorganization of entities responsible for railroad construction and operation in connection with railroad industry structural reform;
3. Formulation of measures for workforce adjustment and securing financial resources in connection with railroad industry structural reform;
4. Revision of statutes and regulations related to railroad industry structural reform;
5. Formulation of railroad industry policies on railroad fares, charges for the use of railroad facilities, railroad transportation markets, etc. in connection with the implementation of railroad industry structural reform;
6. Formulation of government support policies, such as compensation for public service costs and tax and financial support, in connection with the implementation of railroad industry structural reform;
7. Formulation of railroad facilities construction plans and measures for financing investment in connection with the implementation of railroad industry structural reform;
8. Formulation of policies for the development of railroad technologies related to electricity, signaling, rolling stock, etc. in connection with the implementation of railroad industry structural reform;
9. Revision of railroad safety standards and formulation of safety policies in connection with the implementation of railroad industry structural reform;
10. Formulation of policies for establishing inter-Korean and international railroad networks in connection with the implementation of railroad industry structural reform;
11. External negotiations and public relations concerning railroad industry structural reform;
12. Interconnection and coordination of various railroads in connection with the implementation of railroad industry structural reform;
13. Other duties necessary for railroad policies in general related to railroad industry structural reform.
(2) The Planning Group shall consist of one head and members.
(3) The head of the Planning Group shall be appointed by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport from among Grade 3 public officials or public officials in general service belonging to the Senior Civil Service of that Ministry. <Amended on June 12, 2006; February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013>
(4) Where deemed necessary for the performance of the Planning Group's duties, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may request relevant administrative agencies, relevant public corporations such as the Korea Railroad Corporation, authorities established under special Acts such as Korea National Railway, or relevant research institutions to dispatch their public officials, executive officers, employees, or researchers to the Planning Group. <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013; September 10, 2020>
(5) Detailed matters necessary for the organization and operation of the Planning Group shall be determined by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport. <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013>

Article 12 (Requests for Cooperation from Relevant Administrative Agencies, etc.)
Where necessary for the performance of their duties, the Committee and the Working Committee may request cooperation from relevant administrative agencies, organizations, etc., such as the submission of materials or opinions, or have relevant public officials or relevant experts attend meetings of the Committee or the Working Committee to hear their opinions.

Article 13 (Allowances, etc.)
Members of the Committee and the Working Committee who are not public officials, and relevant experts attending meetings of the Committee or the Working Committee, may be paid allowances, travel expenses, and other necessary expenses within budgetary limits.

Article 14 (Detailed Operating Rules)
Matters necessary for the operation of the Committee and the Working Committee, other than those prescribed in this Decree, shall be determined by the chairperson of the Committee following a resolution of the Committee.

Article 15 (Content of the Master Plan for Informatization of the Railroad Industry, etc.)
(1) The master plan for informatization of the railroad industry under Article 12 (1) of the Act shall include the following matters: <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013>
1. Conditions and prospects for informatization of the railroad industry;
2. Objectives and phased implementation plans for informatization of the railroad industry;
3. Costs necessary for informatization of the railroad industry;
4. Plans for collecting and investigating railroad industry information;
5. Matters concerning the circulation of railroad industry information and promotion of its use;
6. Matters concerning support for technology development related to informatization of the railroad industry;
7. Other matters that the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport deems necessary.
(2) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport intends to formulate or amend the master plan for informatization of the railroad industry pursuant to Article 12 (1) of the Act, the Minister shall undergo deliberation by the Committee. <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013>

Article 16 (Duties of the Railroad Industry Information Center, etc.)
(1) The Railroad Industry Information Center under Article 12 (2) of the Act shall perform the following duties:
1. Collection, analysis, dissemination, and publicity of railroad industry information;
2. Monitoring international trends in the railroad industry and supporting international cooperation projects.
(2) The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may, within budgetary limits, subsidize the operating costs of persons who collect, manage, or provide railroad industry information pursuant to Article 12 (2) of the Act. <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013>

